  "status": "draft",
  "experimental": true,
  "description": "Says which routine vaccines are due now and when the others will be: BCG, hepatitis B, DTP, polio, Hib, measles, rubella, mumps and HPV. Cards that propose a vaccine are warnings. Source: Jamaica MOHW EPI Field Guide (January 2024), implemented with 11 unmodified WHO SMART Immunizations decision tables (CQL).",
  "usage": "Needs the patient's birth date and Immunization records coded with the codes of the WHO value sets (WHO, ICD-11, ATC or SNOMED CT). Known differences from Jamaica's schedule: DTP, polio and Hib primary doses at 6, 10 and 14 weeks in WHO versus 6 weeks, 3 and 6 months in Jamaica; second MMR dose at 15 months in WHO versus 18 months; Jamaica's polio and DTP boosters are not covered; pneumococcal and rotavirus vaccines are not in Jamaica's public routine schedule.",
